# Client-safe values baked into the production build by Vite at build time
# (import.meta.env.VITE_*). Same Supabase project as development. Safe to
# commit: the anon key is public-safe by Supabase's design -- Row Level
# Security is the enforced boundary, not key secrecy (see apps/web/.env's
# own comment on these same two values). Used only for Supabase Auth
# (sign-in/session) and the two RLS-protected self-service bootstrap calls;
# every other domain operation goes through packages/backend's /rpc/*
# endpoints (proxied in production via vercel.json's rewrite), never
# straight to Supabase/Postgres.
